<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Cat FAQ</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #0b1020;
      --panel: #11182b;
      --panel-strong: #16213a;
      --border: #2a3552;
      --text: #e7ecff;
      --muted: #a7b2d9;
      --accent: #7aa2ff;
      --accent-strong: #9ab8ff;
      --shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top, #1a2650 0%, transparent 35%),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #0b1020 0%, #090d19 100%);
      color: var(--text);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .skip-link {
      position: absolute;
      left: 1rem;
      top: 1rem;
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #09101f;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-decoration: none;
      transform: translateY(-180%);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
      z-index: 10;
    }

    .skip-link:focus {
      transform: translateY(0);
      outline: 3px solid var(--accent-strong);
      outline-offset: 3px;
    }

    main {
      width: min(920px, calc(100% - 2rem));
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 5.5rem 0 4rem;
    }

    .hero {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      padding: 2rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 24px;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.01));
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 4rem);
      line-height: 1.05;
      letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    }

    .hero p {
      margin: 0;
      max-width: 62ch;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .faq-list {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .example {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 20px;
      background: rgba(17, 24, 43, 0.9);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      overflow: clip;
    }

    .example details {
      display: block;
    }

    summary {
      list-style: none;
      cursor: pointer;
      padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1rem;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    summary::-webkit-details-marker {
      display: none;
    }

    summary::after {
      content: "+";
      flex: none;
      width: 2rem;
      height: 2rem;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--panel-strong);
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
    }

    details[open] summary::after {
      content: "–";
      transform: rotate(180deg);
      background: rgba(122, 162, 255, 0.12);
    }

    summary:hover {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    }

    summary:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: -3px;
    }

    .details {
      padding: 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .details p {
      margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    }

    .details p:first-child {
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    .details strong {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      main {
        width: min(100% - 1rem, 920px);
        padding-top: 4.75rem;
      }

      .hero,
      .example {
        border-radius: 18px;
      }

      .hero,
      summary,
      .details {
        padding-left: 1rem;
        padding-right: 1rem;
      }
    }

    @media (forced-colors: active) {
      :root {
        --bg: Canvas;
        --panel: Canvas;
        --panel-strong: Canvas;
        --border: ButtonBorder;
        --text: CanvasText;
        --muted: CanvasText;
        --accent: Highlight;
        --accent-strong: HighlightText;
      }

      body,
      .hero,
      .example,
      summary::after {
        forced-color-adjust: auto;
        box-shadow: none;
      }

      .skip-link {
        border: 1px solid ButtonBorder;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <h1 id="page-title">Cat FAQ</h1>
      <p>Quick answers to common cat questions, from zoomies and naps to whiskers, purring, and everyday care.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-list" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
      <h2 id="faq-heading" class="sr-only" hidden>Frequently asked questions</h2>

      <div class="example">
        <details>
          <summary>Why do cats sleep so much?</summary>
          <div class="details">
            <p>Cats are natural energy conservers. Their sleep schedule helps them stay ready for short bursts of hunting, climbing, and play.</p>
            <p>Most healthy adult cats sleep around 12 to 16 hours a day, and kittens or older cats can sleep even more.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <details>
          <summary>Why do cats purr?</summary>
          <div class="details">
            <p>Purring often signals contentment, but cats also purr when they are anxious, in pain, or trying to calm themselves.</p>
            <p>Think of it as one of their many communication tools, not a guaranteed sign of happiness.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <details>
          <summary>Are cats really independent?</summary>
          <div class="details">
            <p>Cats can seem self-sufficient, but they still need regular interaction, enrichment, food, water, and vet care.</p>
            <p>Many cats form strong bonds with their people and enjoy routines, playtime, and predictable attention.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <details>
          <summary>What does a cat's tail tell you?</summary>
          <div class="details">
            <p>A cat's tail can signal mood. A relaxed upright tail often means confidence, while a puffed tail can indicate fear or excitement.</p>
            <p>Tail language works best when you read it alongside ears, eyes, posture, and vocalizations.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <details>
          <summary>How can I keep an indoor cat happy?</summary>
          <div class="details">
            <p>Offer climbing spots, scratching surfaces, puzzle feeders, window views, and daily play sessions that mimic hunting patterns.</p>
            <p>Rotate toys and keep litter boxes clean to support a calm, stimulating home environment.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll("details").forEach((details) => {
      details.addEventListener("toggle", () => {
        details.dataset.state = details.open ? "open" : "closed";
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
